<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vibhuti Narayan Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1927–2000</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vibhuti Narayan Singh was the last ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varanasi">Benares</a>, succeeding in 1939 while still a boy. He acceded to the Indian Union after independence, and in 1949 Benares State was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>. He remained a respected patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> learning and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> scholarship, and continued to preside over the month-long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramnagar-ramlila">Ramnagar Ramlila</a> staged at his family's fort.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vibhuti-narayan-singh.jpg" alt="Vibhuti Narayan Singh" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharaja_Vibhuti_Narayan_Singh_of_Banaras.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
